1
00:00:06,830 --> 00:00:13,490
A sports field is a rectangle, 80 metres by 60 metres, with a semicircle on each short end.

2
00:00:13,540 --> 00:00:15,890
The grass needs new seed.

3
00:00:15,940 --> 00:00:23,300
How would you split the field: into a rectangle and a circle, made of two semicircles, or into triangles only?

4
00:00:23,350 --> 00:00:26,520
Pause the video and choose.

5
00:00:26,570 --> 00:00:28,810
A rectangle, and two semicircles.

6
00:00:28,860 --> 00:00:32,960
Together, the two semicircles make one whole circle.

7
00:00:33,010 --> 00:00:34,810
Remember the area formulae.

8
00:00:34,860 --> 00:00:36,860
Rectangle: length times width.

9
00:00:36,910 --> 00:00:39,130
Triangle: half base times height.

10
00:00:39,180 --> 00:00:43,510
Trapezium: half the sum of the parallel sides, times the height.

11
00:00:43,560 --> 00:00:45,500
Circle: pi R squared.

12
00:00:45,550 --> 00:00:48,440
A compound shape is made of simpler shapes.

13
00:00:48,490 --> 00:00:50,820
Split it, find each area, then add.

14
00:00:50,870 --> 00:00:53,630
For holes and cut-outs, subtract.

15
00:00:53,680 --> 00:00:57,000
For the field: the rectangle is 80 by 60.

16
00:00:57,050 --> 00:01:01,910
The circle has a diameter of 60, so its radius is 30.

17
00:01:01,960 --> 00:01:02,600
Your turn.

18
00:01:02,650 --> 00:01:07,060
Find the area of the field, in square metres, to 1 decimal place.

19
00:01:07,110 --> 00:01:10,310
Pause the video and try it.

20
00:01:10,360 --> 00:01:12,490
The rectangle is 4,800.

21
00:01:12,540 --> 00:01:17,140
The circle is pi times 30 squared, about 2,827.4.

22
00:01:17,190 --> 00:01:21,590
The total is about 7,627.4 square metres.

23
00:01:21,640 --> 00:01:30,050
Estimate first: 80 by 60 is 4,800, and the circle is about 3 times 900, which is 2,700.

24
00:01:30,100 --> 00:01:31,510
So about 7,500.

25
00:01:31,560 --> 00:01:34,300
The answer is sensible.

26
00:01:34,350 --> 00:01:35,650
Here is the method.

27
00:01:35,700 --> 00:01:39,260
Step 1: split the shape into simple shapes.

28
00:01:39,310 --> 00:01:42,190
Step 2: find any missing lengths.

29
00:01:42,240 --> 00:01:46,420
Step 3: find each area, then add, or subtract holes.

30
00:01:46,470 --> 00:01:50,640
Step 4: check with an estimate, and give the units.

31
00:01:50,690 --> 00:01:58,140
The end of a shed is a rectangle 6 metres by 4 metres, with a triangular roof of height 2 metres.

32
00:01:58,190 --> 00:02:01,070
24 plus half of 6 times 2, which is 6.

33
00:02:01,120 --> 00:02:03,940
The total is 30 square metres.

34
00:02:03,990 --> 00:02:04,660
Your turn.

35
00:02:04,710 --> 00:02:10,800
A square tile has sides of 20 centimetres, with a round hole of radius 4 centimetres.

36
00:02:10,850 --> 00:02:14,330
What is the area of the tile, to 1 decimal place?

37
00:02:14,380 --> 00:02:17,320
Pause and work it out.

38
00:02:17,370 --> 00:02:19,500
400 minus pi times 16.

39
00:02:19,550 --> 00:02:26,980
That is 400 minus about 50.3, which is about 349.7 square centimetres.

40
00:02:27,030 --> 00:02:30,740
A ring has outer radius 5 and inner radius 2.

41
00:02:30,790 --> 00:02:36,290
Its area is pi times 25 minus 4, which is 21 pi, about 66.0.

42
00:02:36,340 --> 00:02:40,620
An L-shape is made of a 10 by 2 strip and a 2 by 8 strip.

43
00:02:40,670 --> 00:02:42,670
They share a 2 by 2 corner.

44
00:02:42,720 --> 00:02:44,120
Eva finds the area.

45
00:02:44,170 --> 00:02:46,190
Which line is wrong?

46
00:02:46,240 --> 00:02:47,420
Line 1 is wrong.

47
00:02:47,470 --> 00:02:50,680
The 2 by 2 corner is counted twice.

48
00:02:50,730 --> 00:02:53,390
36 minus 4 is 32.

49
00:02:53,440 --> 00:02:58,230
Builders work out compound areas to order flooring, paint and turf.

50
00:02:58,280 --> 00:03:03,250
They usually add about 10 percent extra for cutting and waste.

51
00:03:03,300 --> 00:03:04,610
One last question.

52
00:03:04,660 --> 00:03:09,350
A rectangle 10 by 8 has a 4 by 3 rectangle cut from one corner.

53
00:03:09,400 --> 00:03:10,630
What is the area?

54
00:03:10,680 --> 00:03:14,060
Pause the video and answer.

55
00:03:14,110 --> 00:03:16,930
80 minus 12 is 68.

56
00:03:16,980 --> 00:03:21,330
To remember: split, find each area, then add or subtract.

57
00:03:21,380 --> 00:03:24,610
Two semicircles make one whole circle.

58
00:03:24,660 --> 00:03:27,270
Do not count an overlap twice.

59
00:03:27,320 --> 00:03:29,450
Estimate to check.

60
00:03:29,500 --> 00:03:34,630
Great work! Now practise lesson 7.2 on Camday.
